Building selscan from source
============================

selscan requires a C++17 compiler and zlib. It has been built with GCC 11 (Rocky Linux 9) and Apple clang 16. Normalization is run with `selscan norm`, and there is no separate norm binary.

    cd src
    make            # builds src/selscan (src/selscan.exe on Windows)
    make check      # runs the regression tests in tests/
    make install    # copies selscan to /usr/local/bin (PREFIX=$HOME for ~/bin)
    make clean      # removes src/build/ and the binary

Linux: install a compiler and the zlib headers, e.g. `dnf install gcc-c++ zlib-devel` or `apt install g++ zlib1g-dev`.

macOS: install the Xcode command line tools (`xcode-select --install`).

Windows: install MSYS2 (https://www.msys2.org). In the MINGW64 shell, run `pacman -S make mingw-w64-x86_64-gcc mingw-w64-x86_64-zlib`, then build as above.

Options are given on the make command line, e.g. `make STATIC=1`:

    CXX=...         compiler
    CXXFLAGS=...    compiler flags (default -O3)
    STATIC=1        Linux: link libstdc++, libgcc, and zlib statically (glibc stays dynamic).
                    Windows: a static .exe.
    UNIVERSAL=1     macOS: one binary for Apple Silicon and Intel.
    MACOS_MIN=11.0  macOS: oldest supported macOS version.

For a debug build with the undefined-behavior sanitizer, use
`make CXXFLAGS="-O1 -g -fsanitize=undefined" LDFLAGS=-fsanitize=undefined`.
